{"n": 452, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "452.webp", "text": "2026045\n\n26—1a\n\nPlace Special Too! 26 1 030 and a\nhelping rail (steel ruler) on the\nvibration damper and measure the\nangle of engine inclination.\n\nPlace Special Tool 26 1 030 anda\nhelping rail (steel ruler) on a level\nengine block surface which is\nperpendicular to the crankshaft,\n(For example: M 40 engine)\n\nApply gage on propeller shaft front\nsection and measure angle.\n\nMeasure deflection angle* of joint disc\nand, If necessary, correct it with shims\n(up to max. 3 mm / 0.118\") on the\ntransmission suspension or center\nmount.\n\nExample:\n\nEngine angle 2° 16°\nPropeller shaft angle - 2°06\"\n\nJoint disc defi. angle +0° 10°\n\nApply gage on propeller shaft rear\nsection and measure angie.\n\nDetermine deflection angle* of center\nmount and, If necessary, correct It with\nshims (up to max. 3 mm / 0.118\") on\ntransmission suspension or center\nmount.\n\n* See Specifications\n\nApply gage on final drive with helping\nrall (steel ruler) and measure angle.\nDetermine deflection angle* of the\nuniversal Joint and, if necessary,\ncorrect It with shims (up to max. 3 mm\nor 0.118\") on the center mount.\n\nNote\n\nWhen correcting a deflection angle by\ninstalling shims, remember that the\ndeflection angles of the adjacent joints\nwill also change.\n\nIn general joints should have as smail\nas possible deflection angles.\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["2026045", 0.1955, 0.2765, 0.2432, 0.2851], ["26—1a", 0.4625, 0.0298, 0.5294, 0.0524], ["Place", 0.2791, 0.0703, 0.308, 0.0849], ["Special", 0.3121, 0.0703, 0.3506, 0.0849], ["Too!", 0.3546, 0.071, 0.3774, 0.0822], ["26", 0.382, 0.071, 0.3941, 0.0822], ["1", 0.3987, 0.0716, 0.4022, 0.0816], ["030", 0.4073, 0.0716, 0.4255, 0.0822], ["and", 0.4296, 0.0716, 0.4488, 0.0822], ["a", 0.4529, 0.0736, 0.4585, 0.0822], ["helping", 0.2786, 0.0875, 0.3181, 0.1015], ["rail", 0.3227, 0.0875, 0.3384, 0.0988], ["(steel", 0.343, 0.0882, 0.3708, 0.1008], ["rul